Patch-ID: P-APP-001 (wave-5 slice 2) — DidEndMainMessageLoop bridge
finalization.
Rationale: third milestone of engine/docs/patches/P-APP-001.md, patch-map row
"DidEndMainMessageLoop(): replace its call to AppController.sharedController
with bridge finalization. A teardown-only call to sharedController would
recreate/replace the delegate." When an engine lifecycle host is registered,
AppController was never created (patch app/003 gate), so
ChromeBrowserMainPartsMac::DidEndMainMessageLoop() now finalizes through
rearc::FinalizeReArcAppDelegate() and never touches
AppController.sharedController. Without a host the stock
-[AppController didEndMainMessageLoop] call runs bit-identically.
FinalizeReArcAppDelegate() itself remains the 002 scaffolding no-op (records
the transition via VLOG); ordered tab/keepalive teardown arrives with P-TAB-001
and the remaining P-APP-001 slices.
Gate: rearc::GetEngineLifecycleHost() != nullptr. No new includes: patch
app/003 already imported rearc_app_delegate_mac.h (declares
FinalizeReArcAppDelegate) and rearc_engine_lifecycle.h into this file.
Drift check @ 156.0.8078.74 (2026-11-01): none. The upstream
DidEndMainMessageLoop AppController call moved from
chrome_browser_main_mac.mm:185 (pre-003 pin recording) to :203 after this
patch; rebase notes should target the gated form.
Upstream hunks: chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main_mac.mm only (the gated
finalization block).
Last rebased: 2026-11-01 @ 156.0.8078.74.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main_mac.mm b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main_mac.mm
index e93ab07125..a6eca25a04 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main_mac.mm
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main_mac.mm
@@ -194,5 +194,14 @@
 }
 
 void ChromeBrowserMainPartsMac::DidEndMainMessageLoop() {
+  // P-APP-001 (patch app/004): with an engine lifecycle host registered,
+  // AppController was never created (app/003); requesting sharedController
+  // here would instantiate it during teardown and violate the delegate
+  // identity invariants. Finalize through the bridge instead. Without a
+  // host, the stock AppController path runs unchanged.
+  if (rearc::GetEngineLifecycleHost()) {
+    rearc::FinalizeReArcAppDelegate();
+    return;
+  }
   [AppController.sharedController didEndMainMessageLoop];
 }
